      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it there in the first place.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent: it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or written into the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
